      "In 10,000 transactions, 100 are fraudulent. A model flags 200, of which 80 are fraud. It misses 20 fraud and flags 120 legitimate payments. Precision is 80/200=40%; recall is 80/100=80%. An always-legitimate classifier has 99% accuracy but catches no fraud.",
      "TP=80; FP=120; FN=20; TN=9780\nprecision = 80 / (80 + 120) = 0.40\nrecall = 80 / (80 + 20) = 0.80\naccuracy = (80 + 9780) / 10000 = 0.986\nreview_load = 200 / 10000 = 0.02",
